      "chosen": ["Improve nutrient use efficiency by soil testing, applying nutrients at critical growth stages, and using mycorrhizal fungi.", "Research supports that targeted nutrient management and symbiotic relationships can enhance nutrient uptake and efficiency.", "Techniques include foliar feeding, optimizing compost application, and intercropping with nitrogen-fixing plants."],
      "rejected": ["Improving nutrient use efficiency is too complicated.", "Just apply more fertilizer; efficiency isn't crucial.", "There are no effective techniques for optimizing nutrient use in organic farming."]
    },
